<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	2.2 Examine the available views one by one if necessary, and pick one that is as close as possible to what you want your private view to be.  </run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>For example, if you want a view that includes the supplier, the order originator, the payment method, the status of the order and the commitment number, perhaps the "Orders By Company" view would be a good choice.  </run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	2.3 When you have selected a view, you need to know its name. The View's name is NOT NECESSARILY the same as the name you see in the navigator!  </run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>		2.3.1   Launch the view.  </run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>		2.3.2  The name of the view will be displayed at the top of the screen, like this: </run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
