 pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>3. Using the menu bar at the top, click on Create then select View.  this dialog box will appear:</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	3.1 First, enter a unique name in the first field.  </run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	3.2 Second, click the "Copy From" button.  This is where you will select the name of the view, the one you recorded in step 2.  In this example, I selected the view called "View By Supplier" in the left-hand-side navigator, but whose REAL name is "Order By Company".  Because I LAUNCHED this view in an earlier step, the name of the view is still visible at the top of the screen, in the image I am showing you below.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	3.3  Third, scroll down to the name of the view you want.  You will notice that often there are TWO views by that name.  In this exmaple, on view is called "Order By Company - Current FY" and the other is called "Orders By Company".  The latter will display all of the orders in the database, the former only the orders that were placed this fiscal year.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	Highlight the one you want and then press OK</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	3.4 Fourth click the Customize button, which will launch the View Editor.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run><picture
