<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>			</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>			4.2.4.1 IF YOU DO NOT KNOW THE FIELD NAME YOU WANT</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>				- you can try many fields, one at a time, refreshing the view between each try</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>				- OR you can do this:</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>					- Launch an Order in the application, preferably one that contains recognizable data in the field you are 						interested in.  </run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>					- Right click in the body of the order and select Document Properties</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>					- Scroll down the kist of fields, clicking on each one in turn.  The right-hand-side of the list box will display the 					value assigned to each field, in the selected document.  Keep checking until you find the field that contains the 					data you want.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>					- once you have identified the correct field name, you can close the dialog box and the document.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>					- return to your private view, and do steps 4.2.3 and 4.2.4</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>				For example, if you want to add the Bill To name to your private view:</run></par>
